# Belt to .gitignore's braces.
#
# Deploying from GitHub only ever sends committed files, so .gitignore is enough.
# Deploying with the Vercel CLI uploads the working directory instead, and the
# CLI does not read .gitignore. Without this file, one `vercel` run from a laptop
# that has real household data in data/family.json uploads it. That is the exact
# leak the whole demo-versus-private rule in lib/catalog.ts exists to prevent.
#
# Same shape as .gitignore: ignore the contents, keep the example.
/data/*
!/data/family.example.json

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

cowork/
screenshots/
supabase/
*.md
!README.md
